2026-09-07T11:09:44.1927208Z [36;1m[0m
2026-09-07T11:09:44.1927942Z [36;1m# The following logic implements the configuration priority described in the README:[0m
2026-09-07T11:09:44.1929098Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-09-07T11:09:44.1929477Z [36;1m# Inputs[0m
2026-09-07T11:09:44.1929911Z [36;1m# Environment Variables[0m
2026-09-07T11:09:44.1930393Z [36;1m# Config File[0m
2026-09-07T11:09:44.1930807Z [36;1m# Defaults[0m
2026-09-07T11:09:44.1931187Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-09-07T11:09:44.1931977Z [36;1m# As noted above defaults are awkward to handle as GitHub Actions will inject those values as the input[0m
2026-09-07T11:09:44.1933308Z [36;1m# if the caller doesn't provide them, thus if the input matches the default we don't set it as we[0m
2026-09-07T11:09:44.1935167Z [36;1m# can't tell the difference.  Plus if we did set it when it was the default value then it could potentially[0m
2026-09-07T11:09:44.1937019Z [36;1m# override an external environment variable, or something in the callers configuration file, which then wouldn't[0m
2026-09-07T11:09:44.1938215Z [36;1m# match the configuration priority that is documented.[0m
2026-09-07T11:09:44.1938900Z [36;1mset_env_var_if_provided() {[0m
